      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The risk connotation of terminology in influencing decision-making should not be underestimated. For example, \"superficial\" T1HG bladder cancer has the same poor cancer-specific survival as that conferred by the \"highest risk\" prostate cancer (Gleason 10, T3b). Co-management of concomitant prostate cancer and non-muscle invasive bladder cancer requires a careful competing risk analysis by both the physician and patient. Herein, we detail how patients and physicians should be careful not to underestimate the risk attributed to \"non-muscle invasive\" bladder cancer."
      },
